            <ArticleTitle>[Subjective misconcepts of social status and coronary troubles (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>478-86</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The study of various social parameters as risk factors for coronary diseases gives contradictory results. The inadequacy of social status and the consequent subjective misconcept could reconcile these apparent oppositions. The present research seems to confirm the fact that misconcepts induced by inadequacity of social status are more frequent and more intensive in patients with coronary troubles.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
